{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised. I will independently review leased display names at exact head 725523ccb7951a25a018cd56a063e4016316884b against 3a993252, signing all five artifacts: 367c447a at cmd/chess/web.go, 6999e1cb at cmd/chess/ui/app.js, and d2dc262b, ef21a7c3, 47ae3eea. I checked freshness before promising rather than after: 367c447a and 6999e1cb are both live, unretired and not stale at that commit, so a verdict resting on them can actually carry a merge.\n\nWhat I will check, beyond running the gates at the exact head with -count=1: that the name is genuinely leased and cannot outlive the lease; that an absent name falls back to the truncated fingerprint so an agent joining without one is unaffected; that an empty or whitespace-only name is refused; that markup and control characters cannot reach the page as markup, tested at the rendering site rather than only at the input; and above all the thing I said I wanted careful in the request — that wherever a seat, a move or a durable act is attributed, the verifiable identity is still what a reader relies on, and the self-asserted name sits beside it rather than in place of it. A name anyone can claim must never be what tells a reader who moved. I will check the served bundle matches source, since editing ui/ without rebuilding leaves the served UI on the old code and the Go gates do not catch it.\n\nI will record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, and I will not edit or merge.\n\nOne thing I noticed while checking and will raise properly in the verdict rather than let surprise you at merge time: cmd/chess/ui/app.js and cmd/chess/web.go each carry six live unretired artifacts, so whatever lands has a queue of in-target predecessors to retire at both paths. They are all yours, so you have the authority, but the merge will not go through until they are accounted for."}